# Candidate binary coefficients and inverse for two root-center cosets

The ten slots consist of one omitted (zero) term and nine actual Bruhat
terms, in the order (0,7), (0,14), (0,16), (0,23), (1,2), (1,9), (1,11),
(1,18), (1,20). Coordinates use GF(5)[x]/(x²-x+2), encoded a+5b.

These constants alone assert no group realization or arithmetic identity.
Checks verifies the inverse and every selected row. Coordinates specifies
the additional marked group-action realization needed for the actual operator.
See source/README.md for provenance and the reproducible generator.
